      "source": [
        "### Exploratory-analysis interpretation\n",
        "\n",
        "Density is mathematically constrained by mass and volume, so associations with mean atomic mass and volume per atom are physically expected. Correlation alone does not prove causation.\n",
        "\n",
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "298eec7c",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "298eec7c"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 7. Physics-Informed Feature Engineering\n",
        "\n",
        "Three representations are evaluated:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Composition:** Mean Atomic Mass, Number of Elements, and categorical Chemical System.\n",
        "- **Structure:** Volume per Atom and categorical Crystal System.\n",
        "- **Combined:** all selected composition and structure descriptors.\n",
        "\n",
        "Raw unit-cell volume is excluded because it is extensive and depends on cell size. Number of sites is retained for quality checks but excluded as a predictor because it can reflect crystallographic cell choice. Space-group number is not used as a continuous input.\n",
        "\n",
        "The earlier unused PCA calculation has been removed. With a small, interpretable descriptor set, unevaluated dimensionality reduction would add complexity without scientific benefit."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 11,
      "id": "791ffab7",
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "run-required"
        ],
        "id": "791ffab7",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "9fdba852-da02-4356-ee17-1d4341631a21"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Composition: ['Mean Atomic Mass', 'Number of Elements', 'Chemical System']\n",
            "Structure: ['Volume per Atom', 'Crystal System']\n",
            "Combined: ['Mean Atomic Mass', 'Number of Elements', 'Volume per Atom', 'Chemical System', 'Crystal System']\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# RUN THIS CELL\n",
        "FEATURE_SETS = {\n",
        "    \"Composition\": {\n",
        "        \"numeric\": [\"Mean Atomic Mass\", \"Number of Elements\"],\n",
        "        \"categorical\": [\"Chemical System\"],\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"Structure\": {\n",
        "        \"numeric\": [\"Volume per Atom\"],\n",
        "        \"categorical\": [\"Crystal System\"],\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"Combined\": {\n",
        "        \"numeric\": [\n",
        "            \"Mean Atomic Mass\",\n",
        "            \"Number of Elements\",\n",
        "            \"Volume per Atom\",\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "        \"categorical\": [\"Chemical System\", \"Crystal System\"],\n",
        "    },\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "for feature_set_name, feature_specification in FEATURE_SETS.items():\n",
        "    selected_columns = (\n",
        "        feature_specification[\"numeric\"]\n",
        "        + feature_specification[\"categorical\"]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    print(f\"{feature_set_name}: {selected_columns}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "afc3e6de",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "afc3e6de"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 8. Train–Test Splitting Strategy\n",
        "\n",
        "A random row-level split can place polymorphs or related entries with the same reduced formula in both training and test sets. This notebook uses `GroupShuffleSplit` with reduced formula as the group. Each formula is assigned wholly to training or test data, producing a more demanding estimate for unfamiliar formulas and reducing leakage.\n",
        "\n",
        "The notebook stops explicitly if there are too few formula groups; it does not silently fall back to a row-level split."
      ]
    },
